---
source: tests/help_snapshots.rs
---
Stream the logs of one timeline of a run.

How a run is structured: An Antithesis run is a tree of timelines, not one
history. A timeline is a series of input_hashes. An input_hash is a hash of
every input Antithesis sent up to that point. Antithesis branches a timeline by
sending an input from some moment, which creates a new input_hash. Every event
has an input_hash and a vtime, and one input_hash can have zero or more events.
Events that share an input_hash are on the same timeline. vtime is the virtual
time at which the event was emitted on its timeline. Antithesis virtualizes the
clock, so vtime can jump forward by any amount, but it never goes backward.
vtime orders events only within one timeline.

INPUT_HASH identifies the timeline: the hash of every input Antithesis sent from
the root to that point. Logs stream from the root (or --begin-vtime) to the
timeline's current end; a run in progress can extend the timeline, so the same
INPUT_HASH can return more logs later. Give VTIME to end the stream at that
moment instead. Find a moment with `runs properties --detail`, `runs events`,
`runs search`, or the failure moment of an incomplete run in `runs show`.

Each event has its moment (an input_hash and a vtime), its source, and its
payload: log output, an SDK assertion, a fault, a container lifecycle change, or
a test composer command.

Output: a `moment HASH` divider opens each timeline segment, and each event
under it renders on one line as `VTIME [source] payload`, each event shape in
its own concise form. VTIME is truncated to fit its column, and a long source
label ends in `…`. With --detail, VTIME and the source print whole, and indented
lines under an event give its source location, as `@ file:function:line`, and
the details that it carries, such as an SDK assertion's details, as
`details {...}`.

Add --json for machine-readable output. Each event prints as one JSON object on
its own line:
  snouty --json runs logs <run_id> <hash> | jq -r .moment.vtime

Usage: snouty runs logs [OPTIONS] <RUN_ID> <INPUT_HASH> [VTIME]

Arguments:
  <RUN_ID>
          Run ID

  <INPUT_HASH>
          Input hash identifying the timeline to stream

  [VTIME]
          Virtual time of the moment to end the stream at; omit it to stream to
          the timeline's current end

Options:
      --begin-vtime <BEGIN_VTIME>
          Start from this virtual time instead of the root

  -d, --detail
          Detailed rendering: a full-width vtime on every line, source
          locations, and each event's attached details JSON

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Output JSON where supported (NDJSON for list/stream commands, pretty
          JSON otherwise)

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
